+**The verifier dispatch** (`skills/flow/visual-verify.md`) uses for the verifier's rows.
+`run-verify-list.sh` records the row itself, never the parent by hand: both groups are run with the
+same five trailing arguments, and each records `begin` before its first command and `end -outcome
+completed` after its last when its list exited 0. The first `begin` stamps the start and the later
+group's `end` the finish. A group that exited non-zero records no `end`; once its one inline re-run
+is decided, the parent ends the row itself, `-outcome completed` when the re-run passed, or
+`-outcome blocked -cause <cause>` when a command failed twice — `test-failure` for a command of the
+branch that failed twice, `environment` where the environment itself failed twice (a missing build
+prerequisite).
 
 ```bash
-flow record dispatch begin -change <name> -role verifier -model <parent model> -effort <parent effort> \
-  -agent-id inline -key verify[-<worktree basename>] -session-token mf-<literal-token>
-# … run the list above and write the ## Report — never begin and end in one call …
+run-verify-list.sh <worktree> lint <name> verify[-<worktree basename>] mf-<literal-token> <parent model> <parent effort>
+run-verify-list.sh <worktree> test <name> verify[-<worktree basename>] mf-<literal-token> <parent model> <parent effort>
+# … only after a group exited non-zero and its re-run is decided:
 flow record dispatch end -change <name> -key verify[-<worktree basename>] \
-  -session-token mf-<literal-token> -outcome completed
+  -session-token mf-<literal-token> -outcome completed|blocked [-cause <cause>]
 ```
 
